just a few minutes ago we had a delivery  from Ikea of all of these boxes these  are all bookshelves which are going to  be replacing the kinds of bookshelves we  have been building so far and I am the  one who gets to put them all together so  you see my two main tools that I think  I'm gonna be needing right there and in  a moment I'm going to start opening  these up and seeing what the task ahead  of me looks like well looking at the  boxes it doesn't look like they open  these boxes open up and see what's one  looks like this is gonna be quite a task  I don't know how many of these I'm going  to do today but we shall see so a lot of  boards and  most important part the instructions so  we have eight of these  a bottom piece so now I just have to  figure out how to follow this booklet  directions and get this thing together  looking at all the pictures I figure out  all the hardware does and see what's  what so that's that so after putting in  a good three and a half hours I would  say I've got five units set up the  corner piece three this way one this way  got another one to go there and two to  go along that wall so quite a bit more  yet to do so how do I like these since  this is an unboxing video I mean they  look pretty nice  I got to say I am NOT a fan of having to  handle trim nails banged up my thumb  quite a bit trying to do that the trim  holds this in it's easy to end up  hitting the boards and that sort of  thing so it would be nice if you know  that sort of thing was marked the way  IKEA marks everything else but on the  whole you know it's not totally painless  process certainly not in a room that  small that was you know full of all  sorts of other boxes including the boxes  for these but it's some overall not too  bad you know we've got now five decent  bookshelves we can start loading books  on them which is the whole point of  having bookshelves and start getting on  with turning this into the library that  it's supposed to be so the next thing  that has to go is the bookshelf that I  built it going to disassemble that first  I gotta get all those books off of it  probably putting them  to one of these but before that we've  got to wait till Andy gets back home so  we can figure out exactly how we're  going to bracket this and if I've got  things in precisely the right places  with the underneath brackets I'm not  quite sure about that myself so you know  since we're gonna have to look at it for  quite a while better to get it right the  first time  and then in case I'm knocking off for  the day except for a little bit more to  do once once the gambia gets back here  and maybe we'll start putting some books  on these tomorrow all right these are  all the book shows that are going in  here I've already put some of my own  books that were on the other shelf there  so you can see what IKEA bookshelves  look like when you put them together  creating kind of an octagonal room  because of these middle joint  bookshelves which take up a little bit  of space but actually give us quite a  bit of bookshelf space and they don't  interfere with the room too much so this  is going to be our library and pretty  happy with the way in which the shelves  look although you've got to say looking  at it it looks like the center though  the corner bookshelves are a slightly  different shade of white than the other  bookshelves I'm not sure if that's  actually showing up here but you can see  it with the naked eye perhaps it's just  a function of the fluorescent light that  I'm using right now but it'll have to do  and I'm sure it'll look great after  we've got a lot of the books that need  to go up there on the shelves now that  all the construction is finished with  these a takia bookshelves I've got eight  units in in this room two corner pieces  and six main bookshelves I thought it  would take a little time and talk about  why having a library like this is such  an important thing for  for me and also for a woman that I  married to who's a bibliophile  unfortunate not to have somebody like  that who's supportive having an entire  room devoted to books so you know I  think for a lot of people having a lot  of books and having the the shelving for  it is really a luxury and you know you  go into many people's places and you see  a couple book shelves and you know  that's that's really about yeah and I  think that you know for for most people  that's probably pretty practical you  know you can say when you put two  academics together and two people who  really enjoy their subject matters and  who are essentially omnivorous readers  you're going to have a lot of books but  I think for me part of the reason why  I'm so happy to have all this you know  space to do this is that you know in  many of the places that I've lived that  was a possibility and I'm thinking  specifically about something that made a  huge impression on me as a kid  namely my uncle Hubert's library and my  uncle Hubert is my great uncle on my  adoptive mother's side the Larry's  family and he was a real bibliophile he  was a constant reader well the rest of  the family was doing other stuff he  would retire and read he didn't get to  go to school very long because he was  the oldest of 13 surviving children was  he the oldest no he wasn't quite the  oldest he was pretty close and so being  one of the boys he had to go off during  grade school and start working and he  just kept reading and reading and  reading and he played an incredibly  important role in my mother's generation  for getting some some kids from you know  this part of Chicago or the French  Canadians and Menominee Indians lived  and none of whom you know had thought  about going to college to go to the  library regularly and then to think  about going to call  as a matter of fact it was he and and a  few other relatives who helped my mom to  apply for DePaul and she hadn't done  that she wouldn't have met my father it  was also a first-generation college goer  who was up at the University of  wisconsin-madison at the time and you  know things wouldn't have pianned out  the way they did for not only for myself  but also for a lot of other people in  the family so uncle Hubert he was really  instrumental and when he retired he and  my grandfather and my uncle Ernie  and all of their their wives uncle  Hubert and my grandfather married two  sisters from Quebec grandma and aunt  honey and so they were very very close  as a matter of fact their houses same  house actually Wausau home same model  just slightly different colors we're  joined by a four car garage and then  uncle Ernie built his little ways away  there were actually five brothers who  talked about retiring out there in  Indiana so in any case they had a  basement and uncle Hubert put in shelves  in the basement and he put in this this  really extensive library where I spent a  lot of time as a kid because I would  stay there quite often in the summers  either at Oklahoma and Tony's or at  grandpa and grandmas later on when my  uncle Scott nantan bought uncle Ernie's  place at staying a third place but I  spent a lot of time down there in the  library that was also the common eating  place as well there was a massive  butchers table that could seat about 20  and that's where we had you know  Christmas dinners and Easter dinners and  all sorts of stuff like that just  surrounded by my books like this only  going up to the ceiling and going the  entire you know length of that room so  later on with with my inheritance  I bought uncle Hubert and aunt Tony's  house and that's where I had my office  down in that area for some time there's  a long story about you know where we're  all that's going  tell here long story short I don't I  don't you know that's not my place  anymore but I really loved having those  those bookshelves around and just being  surrounded with with volume so I knew  you know like if I want to go over here  and take one of these that's fine it was  it was a great place to work and so you  know wherever I've lived I've always  been able to put in some bookshelves and  if possible many bookshelves these are  particularly attractive and  well-designed they're not the sort of  cobbled together stuff that I typically  do just because I know much more  utilitarian about it I'm not a design  person but I'm very happy with the look  of them they set off the you know the  white sets off the books quite nicely  but so that's you know part of why for  me putting up these bookshelves is you  might say one of the first parts of  really settling in here you know there's  get the kitchen ready and get the  bathroom ready and you know find a place  where we can you know relax and get the  bedroom you know get the bed set up but  you know for somebody like me this and  having my chalkboard in my desk really  important for my my mindset about this  being a place where I'm going to get a  lot of work done so that's again a  little bit of the backstory of why  bookshelves matter to me so much so you  know all told I'd say I'm pretty happy  with these Billy bookshelves it is quite  a bit of work and you have to really pay  close attention to what you're doing I  found out the hard way and you know  they're pretty heavy to carry so if you  know if you're not all that strong  you're gonna need somebody to actually  move the boxes somewhere for you but  it's it's a manageable task and they  look pretty nice so I'm pretty happy  with them
 

